//! task: write
//! ask: Write a function that is true when x lies outside the interval lo to hi.
//! expect: ok
//! refs: §8.4, §8.6
//! explain: `vel` is the short-circuit disjunction, one level below `et`, and the right operand is evaluated only when the left is false. The comparison words are contextual, so `lt` and `gt` stay ordinary identifiers everywhere except in operator position.

publica functio extra(x: u32, lo: u32, hi: u32) -> u1 {
    si x lt lo vel x gt hi {
        redde 1;
    }
    redde 0;
}
